From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:24:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/36] [AGS] sys_events.cpp: define
 is_sdl_mod_key/make_sdl_mod_flag

Patch 0017 updated these two declarations in sys_events.h to take the
real SDL_KeyboardEvent (SDL_Keysym is gone in SDL3) and moved them from
inline-in-header to declared-here-defined-in-sys_events.cpp -- its own
comment on the declarations already says so -- but the actual
out-of-line definitions were never written, leaving both undefined at
link time. Only surfaced now, by the same continued full build this
session's other new patches came from: Engine/main/game_run.cpp (the
only caller) is one of the files affected by the "never actually
compiled by any prior session" gap this session found in Common/, so
this particular link error was never reached before either, in any
previous session.

Ported directly from the pre-patch-0017 originals (git show
94e271df9:Engine/ac/sys_events.h) rather than guessed: SDL_Keysym's own
scancode field is exactly the same field, now flattened directly onto
SDL_KeyboardEvent (patch 0017's own finding), and the KMOD_* constants
were already renamed SDL_KMOD_* by this same function's sibling
sdl_mod_to_ags_mod() just above and by patch 0020 elsewhere.

Verified: the undefined is_sdl_mod_key(SDL_KeyboardEvent const&)/
make_sdl_mod_flag(SDL_KeyboardEvent const&) references are gone from a
full build.
---
 Engine/ac/sys_events.cpp | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/ac/sys_events.cpp b/Engine/ac/sys_events.cpp
index 160716015..47c8ccdb2 100644
--- a/Engine/ac/sys_events.cpp
+++ b/Engine/ac/sys_events.cpp
@@ -48,6 +48,42 @@ int sdl_mod_to_ags_mod(const Uint16 mod)
     return ags_mod;
 }
 
+// DOS-PORT: patch 0017 updated these two declarations in sys_events.h to
+// take the real SDL_KeyboardEvent (SDL_Keysym is gone in SDL3) and moved
+// them from inline-in-header to declared-here-defined-in-sys_events.cpp
+// -- its own comment on the declarations already says so -- but the
+// actual out-of-line definitions were never written, leaving both
+// undefined at link time (only surfaced now: game_run.cpp is one of the
+// files affected by the "23 never-built files" gap this same continued
+// build found in Common/, so this was never actually reached before
+// either). Ported directly from the pre-patch-0017 originals
+// (git show 94e271df9:Engine/ac/sys_events.h): SDL_Keysym::scancode is
+// exactly the same field, now flattened onto SDL_KeyboardEvent, and the
+// KMOD_* constants were already renamed SDL_KMOD_* by this same patch's
+// own sibling function above and by patch 0020.
+bool is_sdl_mod_key(const SDL_KeyboardEvent &key)
+{
+    return key.scancode == SDL_SCANCODE_LCTRL || key.scancode == SDL_SCANCODE_RCTRL ||
+        key.scancode == SDL_SCANCODE_LALT || key.scancode == SDL_SCANCODE_RALT ||
+        key.scancode == SDL_SCANCODE_LSHIFT || key.scancode == SDL_SCANCODE_RSHIFT ||
+        key.scancode == SDL_SCANCODE_MODE;
+}
+
+int make_sdl_mod_flag(const SDL_KeyboardEvent &key)
+{
+    switch (key.scancode)
+    {
+    case SDL_SCANCODE_LSHIFT: return SDL_KMOD_LSHIFT;
+    case SDL_SCANCODE_RSHIFT: return SDL_KMOD_RSHIFT;
+    case SDL_SCANCODE_LCTRL: return SDL_KMOD_LCTRL;
+    case SDL_SCANCODE_RCTRL: return SDL_KMOD_RCTRL;
+    case SDL_SCANCODE_LALT: return SDL_KMOD_LALT;
+    case SDL_SCANCODE_RALT: return SDL_KMOD_RALT;
+    case SDL_SCANCODE_MODE: return SDL_KMOD_MODE;
+    default: return SDL_KMOD_NONE;
+    }
+}
+
